  #place(top + left, dx: 421.7211608886719pt, dy: 291.56005859375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[), by the late fourteenth ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 306.1064453125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[century the region had fallen under the suzerainty of the East Javanese empire of Majapahit ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 320.65234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[before degenerating into an autonomous outpost dominated by overseas Chinese armed fleets. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 335.1982421875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Ma Huan’s account documents a pivotal historical intervention: during the first expedition ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 349.74462890625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[(1405–1407), the Ming armada forcibly subdued the entrenched Chinese pirate syndicate ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 364.29150390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[commanded by Chen Zuyi, executing its leadership and establishing an imperial pacification ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 378.83740234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[bureau under a recognized local Chinese merchant headman, Shih Chin-ch'ing. Ma Huan ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 393.38330078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[captures a unique amphibious urban environment where commoners lived upon floating timber ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 407.93017578125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[rafts, local warriors specialized in riverine boat warfare, and lucrative trades in resinous ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 422.4765625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[aromatics, exotic avians, and forest goods were transacted using Ming copper currency. ]]
