  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 72.55615234375pt)[#text(size: 17.0pt)[PART II: ESSAY & HISTORICAL ACCOUNT ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 98.90576171875pt)[#text(size: 13.0pt)[Geographic Approach and Coastal Navigation ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 120.03173828125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Sailing southwest across the sea from Qui Nhon in Champa for seven days with a favorable ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 134.57763671875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[wind brought ships to the maritime approaches of Siam. Entering the shallow waters near the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 149.12451171875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[river estuary at New Strait Towers, vessels anchored in sheltered roadsteads before smaller ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 163.67041015625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[craft navigated the inland waterways toward the royal capital at Ayutthaya. Ma Huan notes that ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 178.21728515625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[the outer frontiers of the kingdom were bordered by rugged hills, while the inland basin ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 192.76220703125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[consisted of low-lying floodplains subject to seasonal inundation. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 219.37451171875pt)[#text(size: 13.0pt)[The Capital, Monarchy, and Monastic Culture ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 240.50048828125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[The royal palace at Ayutthaya featured clean, orderly enclosures, while the dwellings of ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 255.04638671875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[commoners were raised on wooden piles using areca-palm flooring and thatch roofing. The ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 269.59228515625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[monarch, described as adhering devoutly to the Buddhist faith, wore white cloth wrappings on ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 284.13916015625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[his head, draped his shoulders in embroidered silks, and traveled mounted atop elephants or in ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 298.68603515625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[sedan-chairs sheltered by gilded umbrellas. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 325.23095703125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Theravada Buddhism occupied a central place in the civic and religious life of the kingdom. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 339.77783203125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Monks and nuns were numerous, wearing simple robes and residing in extensive monastery ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 354.32470703125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[complexes where they engaged in daily recitations, fasting, and austere disciplines. In civic ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 368.87060546875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[affairs, women exercised substantial autonomy and managed the majority of commercial ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 383.41650390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[negotiations and domestic financial decisions, earning praise from Chinese observers for their ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 397.96240234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[enterprise and intellectual capability. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 424.57373046875pt)[#text(size: 13.0pt)[Social Customs, Domestic Rites, and Funerary Practices ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 445.69970703125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Marriages were arranged with the assistance of Buddhist priests, who escorted the groom to the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 460.24658203125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[household of the bride's parents. Following the initial consummation at her family's dwelling, the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 474.79150390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[groom's kin organized processions with decorated boats, feast preparations, and musical ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 489.33935546875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[accompaniment to conduct the couple back home. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 515.88525390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Funerary customs reflected social station. Wealthy families preserved the remains of deceased ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 530.43115234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[relatives with quicksilver before subterranean burial. Commoners, by contrast, carried their dead ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 544.97705078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[to coastal sands or wild outskirts, leaving the remains exposed to large scavenger birds in a ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 559.52392578125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[practice termed "bird-burial". Once the flesh was consumed, the surviving kin gathered the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 574.07080078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[bones, conducted Buddhist liturgies, and consigned the remains to the river currents. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 600.68115234375pt)[#text(size: 13.0pt)[Inland Trade at Lopburi and Market Commodities ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 621.80810546875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Roughly sixty miles north of the royal capital lay the bustling inland trading center of Lopburi ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 636.35400390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[(]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 75.66048431396484pt, dy: 636.35400390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Shang-shui]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 131.27085876464844pt, dy: 636.35400390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[), accessible by river craft. This market town hosted hundreds of foreign merchant ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 650.89990234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[households and served as a major transshipment hub for valuable forest goods, including ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 665.44580078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[gemstones, cardamoms, chaulmoogra seeds, dragon's-blood resin, and laka-wood. In ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 679.99267578125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[exchange, Chinese traders offered cast iron pans, ceramics, and silk-gauze textiles. ]]
]
