  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 163.67041015625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[southwest, while dense jungle and rugged ranges lay inland to the north and east. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 190.21728515625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Originally, the settlement lacked royal status and was known among maritime traders as the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 204.76220703125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Five Islands. Ruled by a local chieftain, the community was subject to the hegemony of Siam, ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 219.30908203125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[yielding an annual tributary payment of forty ounces of gold under threat of armed raids. During ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 233.85595703125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[the early Yongle period, the Ming court intervened, dispatching Admiral Zheng Ho with imperial ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 248.40185546875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[edicts, royal insignia, and a memorial stone tablet to elevate the chieftain to the rank of king. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 262.94775390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Strengthened by Chinese imperial protection, the newly founded kingdom ceased paying tribute ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 277.49365234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[to Siam and became a sovereign maritime power. The monarch subsequently journeyed to the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 292.04150390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[imperial court in China to present local tribute and express gratitude for imperial investiture. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 318.65185546875pt)[#text(size: 13.0pt)[Urban Infrastructure and the Chinese Depot ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 339.77783203125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[The port town developed around the mouth of the Malacca River. Across the water, the king ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 354.32470703125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[constructed a substantial wooden bridge lined with more than twenty covered booths where ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 368.87060546875pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[merchants gathered daily to barter goods. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 395.41650390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Whenever the Ming treasure ships arrived, Chinese officers established a heavily fortified transit ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 409.96240234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[cantonment surrounded by a double line of palisades and watchtowers. Within these stockades, ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 424.50830078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[armed sentries struck night watches, while expansive storehouses and granaries protected ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 439.05517578125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[provisions, precious metals, and trade goods. When secondary squadrons detached from the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 453.60205078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[main fleet sailed to India, Arabia, or Africa, they returned to this depot, waiting in safety until the ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 468.14697265625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[favorable southwest monsoon allowed the combined armada to set sail for China. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 494.76025390625pt)[#text(size: 13.0pt)[Religion, Attire, and Domestic Society ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 515.88525390625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[The ruler, administrative chiefs, and populace adhered to the Islamic faith, observing daily ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 530.43115234375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[prayers, fasting, and ceremonial liturgies. The monarch wore fine white headcloths, flowing ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 544.97705078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[robes of patterned blue fabric, and soft leather footwear, traveling through the town in wooden ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 559.52392578125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[sedan-chairs. The common people wrapped their heads in cloth squares, wore short coats, and ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 574.07080078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[secured cotton waistcloths (]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 207.63113403320312pt, dy: 574.07080078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[sarongs]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 246.7371368408203pt, dy: 574.07080078125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[) around their bodies. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 600.61572265625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Domestic residences were constructed on raised piles several feet above the ground, using split ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 615.16259765625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[coconut timber for floors and woven mats of screw-pine leaves (]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 382.96942138671875pt, dy: 615.16259765625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[kajang]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 415.3609313964844pt, dy: 615.16259765625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[) for roofs and partitions. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 629.70947265625pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[Agriculture was limited due to sandy and saline soils, prompting the community to rely on ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 644.25537109375pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[fishing, coastal foraging, and imported rice from Sumatra and Java. To supplement their ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 658.80126953125pt)[#text(size: 11.0pt)[sustenance, the populace processed the pulp of sago trees into edible flour cakes. ]]
  #place(top + left, dx: 72.0pt, dy: 685.41259765625pt)[#text(size: 13.0pt)[ ]]
]
